/-! # The stabilizer of a semisimple tangent vector

Source: Milne, Algebraic Groups (2017), Proposition 17.76, printed p.377
(blueprint: lem-sfb-semisimple-tangent-stabilizer).

The adjoint fixed-point condition is written intrinsically as conjugation fixing the
scalar-extended infinitesimal point of X. By the normalization, naturality and conjugation
clauses of AffineGroupDualNumberCalculus.Data, this is exactly Ad(g)(1 tensor X) = 1 tensor X.
Thus no choice of an adjoint representation or of a tangent-space identification enters the
statement. The image condition on points is natural, since the representing map is a morphism.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u v

open CategoryTheory
open scoped TensorProduct MonObj

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- The adjoint stabilizer of a geometrically diagonalizable identity tangent vector is a
smooth closed subgroup, with tangent image the bracket centralizer.
Source: Milne, Algebraic Groups (2017), Proposition 17.76, printed p.377; Proposition 17.74
for the faithful-matrix interpretation (blueprint: lem-sfb-semisimple-tangent-stabilizer).

Proof (the seven steps of the DAG node):
1. In the affine coordinate algebra A of G, put M = di(X) and let I be generated by the
entries of UM - MU for the universal matrix U. Then C = Spec(A/I) is closed in G and its
R-points are precisely the matrices commuting with M, by the affine-spectrum correspondence.
2. The affine-group dual-number calculus gives injectivity of di, also after tensoring with
R: a linear left inverse over k extends to R. Its adjoint equivariance and the matrix tangent
formula identify these equations with Ad(g)(1 tensor X) = 1 tensor X. Equivalently conjugation
fixes the actual scalar-extended dual-number point used below. This works for nonreduced R.
3. Commuting matrices are closed under identity, multiplication and inverse. Applying this
to the universal points over (A/I) tensor (A/I) and A/I makes the Hopf maps descend; their group
diagrams follow from those of G and pointwise injectivity. This gives a closed subgroup C.
4. Conjugation inside G by the infinitesimal point of X induces the derivation D on A with
D(U) = MU - UM and D(det(U) inverse) = 0. Its value ideal is I, since these coordinates generate.
5. Over the algebraic closure, diagonalize M. The transformed matrix coordinates are
eigenvectors of D with weights lambda_a - lambda_b; inverse determinant has weight zero.
Monomials are eigenvectors and span A. Polynomial spectral projectors on finitely many
weights show that the sum of eigenspaces is direct, in every characteristic.
6. Apply lem-sfb-semisimple-derivation-zero-smooth to this derivation on the smooth finite-type
algebra A. Its geometrically split eigenspaces and value ideal I give smoothness of Spec(A/I)
over k, including imperfect fields.
7. A tangent point 1 + epsilon*di(Y) belongs to C precisely when di(Y)M - Mdi(Y) = 0.
The affine-group Lie-tangent calculus identifies this with di([Y,X]) = 0. Injectivity of di
then gives [Y,X] = 0 and the asserted image equality. For X = 0, I = 0 and C = G.
-/
theorem exists_semisimple_tangent_stabilizer
    {k : Type u} [Field k] (K : Type v) [Field K] [Algebra k K] [IsAlgClosure k K]
    (G : Grp (Over (Spec (.of k))))
    [IsAffine G.X.left] [Smooth G.X.hom] [ConnectedSpace G.X.left]
    [LocallyOfFiniteType G.X.hom] [QuasiCompact G.X.hom]
    (n : ℕ) (hn : 1 ≤ n)
    (i : G.X ⟶ GeneralLinearGroup (ULift.{u} (Fin n)) k)
    [IsMonHom i] [IsClosedImmersion i.left] (X : GrpObj.Lie G.X)
    (hX : ∃ (P : Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup (ULift.{u} (Fin n)) K)
      (d : ULift.{u} (Fin n) → K),
      (↑P⁻¹ : Matrix (ULift.{u} (Fin n)) (ULift.{u} (Fin n)) K) *
        (GeneralLinearGroup.RationalHom.differential i X).map (algebraMap k K) *
        (↑P : Matrix (ULift.{u} (Fin n)) (ULift.{u} (Fin n)) K) = Matrix.diagonal d) :
    ∃ (C : Grp (Over (Spec (.of k)))) (j : C ⟶ G),
      IsClosedSubgroupScheme j.hom.hom ∧ Smooth C.X.hom ∧
      (∀ (R : Type u) [CommRing R] [Algebra k R],
        Set.range (fun c : points C.X R ↦ c ≫ j.hom.hom) =
          {g : points G.X R |
            points.map G.X (TrivSqZeroExt.inlAlgHom k R R) g *
                points.map G.X
                  (DualNumber.lift ⟨(Algebra.ofId k (DualNumber R), DualNumber.eps),
                    DualNumber.eps_mul_eps, fun _ ↦ Commute.all _ _⟩)
                  (GrpObj.tangentPoint X) *
                (points.map G.X (TrivSqZeroExt.inlAlgHom k R R) g)⁻¹ =
              points.map G.X
                (DualNumber.lift ⟨(Algebra.ofId k (DualNumber R), DualNumber.eps),
                  DualNumber.eps_mul_eps, fun _ ↦ Commute.all _ _⟩)
                (GrpObj.tangentPoint X)}) ∧
      Set.range (GrpObj.differential j.hom.hom) = {Y : GrpObj.Lie G.X | ⁅Y, X⁆ = 0} := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
